# Copy to .env.local and fill in what you need. Everything here is optional —
# the site runs without any of it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Guardian app map (/experience-app)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The map is drawn from raster tiles on real coordinates. With nothing set it
# uses OpenStreetMap, which needs no key and carries real Korean road, park and
# place data, so the experience works out of the box.
#
# To point it at another raster source, set both of these. The URL template
# takes {z}, {x} and {y}, and the attribution is whatever that provider's
# licence requires — do not ship tiles without it.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MAP_TILE_URL="https://tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png"
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MAP_ATTRIBUTION="© OpenStreetMap contributors"

# Kakao Maps and Naver Maps are vector SDKs rather than tile URLs, so they need
# a small amount of extra wiring on top of the above. Both also require the
# deployed domain to be registered in the provider's console before a key will
# return anything. Add the key here first if you want to go that route:
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_KAKAO_MAP_KEY=""

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Waitlist
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where the waitlist form posts. Unset, submissions are validated and resolved
# locally without leaving the browser.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_WAITLIST_ENDPOINT=""

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3D model
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Set to 1 to load public/models/cane.glb instead of the procedural cane.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CANE_MODEL=""
